  "Name": "ShokoohSaremi2004-Cband-cube-PBS-GA-gradient",
  "Source": "M. Shokooh-Saremi, M. Nourian, M. M. Mirsalehi, S. H. Keshmiri, \"Design of multilayer polarizing beam splitters using genetic algorithm,\" Optics Communications 233, 57-65 (2004). doi:10.1016/j.optcom.2004.01.008 - Table 2, column GA + gradient (p. 63); method text p. 62",
  "Notes": "C-band cube polarizing beam splitter: 200-generation GA result refined by global gradient optimization\nSpecification: Same as GA design; 17-layer GA result (200 generations) optimized with global gradient method, 100 iterations.\nReported: 17 layers; sum d = 4.3471 um; sum(nd) = 7.6104 um (as printed; see notes); P over band: max 1.0, min 0.9898, mean 0.9968, std 0.0028; yield 9 %.\nNotes: Table order is incident (A) -> substrate (S), kept as is. Angstrom converted to nm. Recomputed sum d = 4.3471 um matches the table, but recomputed sum(nd) = 7.4106 um vs printed 7.6104 um (looks like a digit transposition in the paper); layer values themselves are taken as printed.\nLayers from Table 2, column GA + gradient (p. 63); method text p. 62; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours total 4347.1 nm; P min 0.9898, mean 0.9962; paper total 4347.1 nm; P min 0.9898, mean 0.9968.",
